  "summary": "Traditional attire and body decoration worn during Xhosa initiation ceremonies and cultural rites of passage.",
  "description": "Characterized by distinctive white clay (imithi) body paint applied in geometric patterns, combined with traditional garments including blankets, beads, and animal skins. This aesthetic serves to mark the transition to adulthood, with specific designs and colors indicating the wearer's status, gender, and stage within the initiation process, reflecting cultural identity and spiritual beliefs.",
